# Copy to .env and adjust. .env is gitignored -- it describes one machine.

# Working set: lake, derived artefacts, tiles, DuckDB. Put this on the fastest local
# filesystem you have, and NOT on a mounted Windows drive if you are in WSL -- small-file
# operations there are ~100x slower, which is exactly how DuckDB reads partitioned
# Parquet. Defaults to ~/migratlas-data.
# MIGRATLAS_DATA_DIR=/home/you/migratlas-data

# Raw archives: written once, read sequentially once. Safe to put on a big slow disk.
# The Dark Ecology radar archive alone is ~49 GB. Defaults to $MIGRATLAS_DATA_DIR/raw.
# See docs/adr/0004-storage-layout.md for the measurements behind the split.
# MIGRATLAS_RAW_DATA_DIR=/mnt/bulk/migratlas/raw

# Credentials, only for the sources that need them. Never commit real values.
# MIGRATLAS_CRED_EBIRD_API_KEY=
# MIGRATLAS_CRED_MOVEBANK_USER=
# MIGRATLAS_CRED_MOVEBANK_PASSWORD=

# Copernicus Climate Data Store personal access token, from
# https://cds.climate.copernicus.eu/profile. Only needed outside North America: the radar
# driver panel uses NARR, which covers the CONUS domain and needs no credential at all
# (docs/adr/0006). Note the token is necessary but not sufficient -- each dataset's licence
# has to be accepted once from its download tab, or retrieval returns 403.
# MIGRATLAS_CRED_CDS_TOKEN=
